<title>GERMANY: TENNIS-MERCEDES CUP FIRST ROUND RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-MERCEDES CUP FIRST ROUND RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>STUTTGART, Germany 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>First round results</p>
<p>from the $1 million ATP Mercedes Cup men's tournament on Monday:</p>
<p>Karim Alami (Marocco) beat Jiri Novak (Czech Republic) 7-6</p>
<p>(7-1) 4-6 7-5</p>
<p>Fabrice Santoro (France) beat Marcelo Filippini (Uruguay) 7-6</p>
<p>(11-9) 6-3</p>
<p>Jens Knippschild (Germany) beat Martin Damm (Czech Republic)</p>
<p>6-3 4-6 6-4</p>
<p>Slava Dosedel (Czech Republic) beat Dominik Hrbaty (Slovakia)</p>
<p>7-6 (7-4) 6-2.</p>
<p>Marc Goellner (Germany) beat Richey Reneberg (U.S.) 4-6 7-5</p>
<p>1-0, Reneberg retired with back problems</p>
<p>Martin Sinner (Germany) beat Thomas Johansson (Sweden) 6-7</p>
<p>(2-7) 7-6 (7-6) 7-5.</p>
<p>Filip Dewulf (Belgium) beat Bernd Karbacher (Germany)  6-4 1-0,</p>
<p>Karbacher retired with injury to his right shoulder.</p>
</text>
